# Human-Like Chess AI System

This plan outlines the architecture for a "Humanoid" AI mode that feels like a real opponent rather than a machine. It uses Stockfish for tactical move generation (MultiPV) and Leela Chess Zero for background analysis of the user's playstyle to adapt the AI's personality.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This system introduces a significant change to how AI moves are calculated and selected. Instead of always choosing the best move, the AI will now probabilistically select from top candidates based on its current "Personality".

> [!NOTE]
> Background analysis by Leela Chess Zero will run asynchronously after each player move to assess their playstyle (Aggressive, Defensive, etc.) without blocking the UI.

