### 2. Personality & Move Selection (Logic Layer)

#### [NEW] [personality_engine.dart](file:///d:/PP942920DRIVE/PROJECTS/chess/app/lib/domain/engine/personality_engine.dart)
- Define `AIPersonality` enum: `aggressive`, `defensive`, `tricky`, `lazy`, `random`.
- Logic to adapt personality based on user move analysis:
    - User Aggressive (high pressure moves) -> AI Defensive.
    - User Defensive (solid, slow moves) -> AI Aggressive.
    - User Lazy (suboptimal, repetitive moves) -> AI Tricky.
    - User Blunder -> AI Lazy (intentionally plays some random moves).

#### [NEW] [move_selector.dart](file:///d:/PP942920DRIVE/PROJECTS/chess/app/lib/domain/engine/move_selector.dart)
- Implement `selectMove(List<MoveCandidate> candidates, AIPersonality personality)`.
- **Scoring System**: `finalScore = engineScore + personalityBonus + randomness`.
    - `Aggressive`: Bonus for captures, checks, and moves targeting king.
    - `Defensive`: Bonus for safe squares and reinforcing threatened pieces.
    - `Tricky`: Probabilistically selects slightly suboptimal moves if they create "traps" (high variance in follow-up lines).
- Implements the "Human Error System":
    - 20% random legal move chance for `hard` (if applicable), 0% for `impossible`.

